---
import Layout from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import PhotoJournal from "../components/PhotoJournal.astro";
import { journalPhotos } from "../lib/photos";
import { base } from "../lib/site";

const becoming = journalPhotos.slice(0, 6);
const familiar = journalPhotos.slice(6, 10);
const littleThings = journalPhotos.slice(10, 12);
const somewhereNew = journalPhotos.slice(12, 14);
---
<Layout
  title="The Days in Between"
  description="A photographic journal by Jade Zhao · 赵郎溪. Fourteen ordinary days from IU, Indiana, and Madrid."
  canonical="https://zhao-langxi.github.io/zhao-langxi/days.html"
  current="days"
  bodyClass="journal-page"
>
  <main id="main" tabindex="-1">
    <header>
      <p>A photographic journal by Jade Zhao · 赵郎溪</p>
      <h1>The Days in Between</h1>
    </header>
    <article>
      <div class="journal-lede">
        <p>
          I used to think photographs were for the big things. The places you travel to, the people
          you meet, and the moments you know you'll want to remember.
        </p>
        <p>But looking through my camera roll, I keep coming back to the ordinary days.</p>
        <p>
          A walk across campus. A restaurant booth. Flowers growing beside a building. A street in
          Madrid that probably looked completely unremarkable to everyone else.
        </p>
        <p>
          I grew up in Indiana, went to college not too far from home, and eventually found myself
          studying across the ocean. Somewhere between those places, I started collecting little
          pieces of everyday life.
        </p>
        <p>
          These photographs aren't really about where I've been. They're about the things I noticed
          while I was there.
        </p>
        <p>
          And maybe that's what <span lang="zh-Hans">小猫钓鱼</span> means to me now: learning to
          stay with the moment long enough to see what's right in front of me.
        </p>
      </div>

      <section aria-labelledby="becoming-heading">
        <h2 id="becoming-heading">Indiana University · Becoming</h2>
        <PhotoJournal photos={becoming} variant="masonry" idPrefix="becoming" eagerCount={2} />
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="familiar-heading">
        <h2 id="familiar-heading">Indiana · The Familiar Things</h2>
        <PhotoJournal photos={familiar} variant="masonry" idPrefix="familiar" eagerCount={1} />
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="little-heading">
        <h2 id="little-heading">The Little Things · Paying Attention</h2>
        <PhotoJournal photos={littleThings} variant="masonry" idPrefix="little" eagerCount={1} />
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="spain-heading">
        <h2 id="spain-heading">Spain · Somewhere New</h2>
        <PhotoJournal photos={somewhereNew} variant="masonry" idPrefix="somewhere" eagerCount={1} />
      </section>

      <section class="journal-close" aria-labelledby="note-heading">
        <h2 id="note-heading">A Small Note to Myself</h2>
        <p>
          I don't think I took these photographs knowing exactly what they would mean later.
        </p>
        <p>
          Some were taken because the light was nice. Others because something looked familiar,
          funny, or worth remembering for reasons I couldn't quite explain.
        </p>
        <p>Looking back, I like that they're ordinary.</p>
        <p>
          They remind me that growing up isn't always one big turning point. Sometimes it's a
          collection of little moments that only start making sense when you put them together.
        </p>
        <p>And I'm still collecting them.</p>
      </section>

      <p>
        <a href={`${base}iu.html`}>IU</a>
        <a href={`${base}indiana.html`}>Indiana</a>
        <a href={`${base}spain.html`}>Spain</a>
        <a href={`${base}`}>Home</a>
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
